<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galerius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 258–311</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galerius was a Roman emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetrarchy">Tetrarchy</a>, made Caesar under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a> in 293 and senior emperor in the east from 305 to 311. He fought on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> against the Carpi and other peoples and won a major victory over the Persian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narseh">Narseh</a> in 298. A leading force behind the Great Persecution of Christians, he ended it by an edict of toleration shortly before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galerius.jpg" alt="Galerius" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shinjirod · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Romuliana_Galerius_head.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
